HdaCodecHdaIoStreamCallback is called through EFI_HDA_IO_STREAM_CALLBACK
(an EFIAPI function pointer) but was defined with the native SysV
convention, so it read its arguments from the wrong registers and
jumped into the EFI_AUDIO_IO_PROTOCOL struct (#UD) when a stream ended.

diff --git a/Platform/AudioDxe/HdaCodec/HdaCodecAudioIo.c b/Platform/AudioDxe/HdaCodec/HdaCodecAudioIo.c
index 1a2fb12..5e5fc61 100644
--- a/Platform/AudioDxe/HdaCodec/HdaCodecAudioIo.c
+++ b/Platform/AudioDxe/HdaCodec/HdaCodecAudioIo.c
@@ -27,6 +27,7 @@
 
 // HDA I/O Stream callback.
 VOID
+EFIAPI
 HdaCodecHdaIoStreamCallback(
     IN EFI_HDA_IO_PROTOCOL_TYPE Type,
     IN VOID *Context1,
